# EXAMPLE-owned process recipe for the klink imaging starters.
# klink ships NO recipes: this file is a process description YOU write
# (or have an agent write with you) and edit into your own flow.
#
# It is a simplified planar CMOS flow — n-well, LOCOS isolation, gate
# stack, LDD + spacer + source/drain, tungsten plugs, damascene metal-1
# — written so every step is visible in a cross-section.
#
# `# klink-step: <name>` markers cut the recipe into frames: each marker
# names the step that FOLLOWS it, and imaging.xsection_run(steps=True)
# renders the recipe prefix up to each marker. Materials assigned to a
# variable are auto-output under that name, so no output() lines are
# needed here.
#
# NOTE: .pyxs recipes are trusted Python code executed in-process.
#
# Verb semantics (a common authoring trip-up): PATTERNED deposition is
# mask(l).grow(...) — there is no mask(l).deposit(); deposit(...) is
# always a BLANKET (whole-surface) operation. etch(...) is blanket too;
# patterned etch is mask(l).etch(...). grow(..., on=material) grows only
# on top of that material; diffuse(...) drives dopant into a material
# and can be told to pass `through=` a covering film.

delta(5 * dbu)

# mask layers — these are the GDS layers of demo_layout.py
lnwell = layer("1/0")
lactive = layer("2/0")
lpoly = layer("3/0")
lcontact = layer("4/0")
lmetal1 = layer("6/0")
lfield = lactive.inverted()          # everything outside active = field

# klink-step: p-substrate
pbulk = bulk()

# klink-step: n-well implant
# the well is driven deep and pulled slightly inside the mask edge; it
# consumes the p-bulk it grows into
nwell = mask(lnwell).grow(0.55, -0.05, mode='round', into=pbulk)

# klink-step: LOCOS field oxide
# grown twice from ONE derived mask (same seed for both contributions);
# the two halves are named with a leading _ so they stay intermediates
# instead of becoming materials of their own:
# upwards into air and downwards into silicon, then joined — the classic
# half-up/half-down LOCOS profile
mfield = mask(lfield)
_fox_up = mfield.grow(0.22, 0.22, bias=0.12, mode='round')
_fox_dn = mfield.grow(0.22, 0.22, bias=0.12, mode='round',
                     into=[pbulk, nwell])
fox = _fox_up.or_(_fox_dn)

# klink-step: gate oxide
gox = deposit(0.02)

# klink-step: poly gate + silicide
poly = mask(lpoly).grow(0.16, -0.04, mode='round')
silicide = grow(0.08, on=poly)

# klink-step: LDD implants
# shallow, self-aligned to the gate; `through=gox` lets the dopant pass
# the gate oxide instead of stopping on it
nldd = diffuse(0.05, 0.02, into=pbulk, through=gox, bias=0.01,
               mode='round')
pldd = diffuse(0.05, 0.02, into=nwell, through=gox, bias=0.01,
               mode='round')

# klink-step: spacer
# conformal deposition followed by an anisotropic etch-back leaves
# material only on the gate sidewalls
spacer = deposit(0.06, 0.06)
etch(0.06, into=spacer)

# klink-step: source/drain implants
nsd = diffuse(0.12, -0.05, into=[nldd, pbulk], through=gox, mode='round')
psd = diffuse(0.12, -0.05, into=[pldd, nwell], through=gox, mode='round')
etch(0.02, into=[gox, spacer])        # strip oxide off the contacts

# klink-step: ILD deposition
ild = deposit(0.55, 0.55, mode='round')

# klink-step: contact etch + W plug + CMP
# taper gives the holes a 5 degree sidewall; the CMP takes the tungsten
# overburden back down to the ILD, leaving isolated plugs
mask(lcontact).etch(0.85, into=ild, taper=5)
tungsten = deposit(0.18, 0.18)
planarize(into=[tungsten, ild], less=0.5)

# klink-step: metal-1 damascene
imd = deposit(0.22)
mask(lmetal1).etch(0.32, into=imd, taper=5)
metal1 = deposit(0.22, 0.22)
planarize(into=[metal1], less=0.22)
